<div class="note">Withheld for this artifact class (Operational incident assessment): lessons learned. unpromoted candidate — an operational assessment may exist while the incident is active; suspected/undetermined findings are allowed and lessons-learned editing is not</div>




<div class="pmh">1 · Executive summary</div>


<section>
  <h2>Incident at a glance</h2>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">Where it happened</span><span class="v">Not localized — the evidence does not support a single location</span>
    <span class="k">What possibly happened</span><span class="v">No cause hypothesis has supporting evidence yet — the anomaly is recorded without a claimed cause.</span>
    <span class="k">Possible owner(s)</span><span class="v">Application team</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">named by the &#34;Application / service experience change&#34; hypothesis (suspected)</span>
  </div>
  
  <div class="note"></div>
  
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Management summary</h2>
  <div class="mgmt">At 2026-07-12 18:12:00 UTC, One automated check detected a condition of “application / service experience change” affecting crm-portal. The condition is ongoing (1h 48m elapsed). Synthetic path impact is confirmed; actual real-user impact was not confirmed because relevant real-traffic telemetry was insufficient. The cause remains unconfirmed because independent evidence classes did not corroborate the observations. Decision: Investigate — Evidence is aligned but not independently confirmed. Validate the missing evidence before opening a customer incident. Escalation follows the policy thresholds stated in the decision section.</div>
  <div class="note">Confidence basis: evidence rests on One evidence class from one observer. Incident severity: WARN — complete synthetic path loss; single uncorroborated evidence stream (severity capped). <span style="color:#94a3b8">(evidence-peak severity: peak of the attached evidence, carried by synthetic http failure (3 high of 3 anomalous observations))</span></div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Key facts</h2>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">First observed</span><span class="v">2026-07-12 18:12:00 UTC</span>
    
    
    <span class="k">Duration</span><span class="v">1h 48m (elapsed — still active)</span>
    
    
    
    <span class="k">Root cause</span><span class="v">Not identified — no cause hypothesis has supporting evidence yet</span>
  </div>
</section>


<div class="pmh">2 · Impact</div>
<section>
  <p style="margin:4px 0 8px;font-weight:600">Synthetic-transaction impact confirmed: the configured checks failed from their vantages. Real-user impact is a separate axis (not observable) and is never derived from synthetic failures.</p>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">Synthetic-transaction axis</span><span class="v">Confirmed</span>
    <span class="k">Real-user axis</span><span class="v">Not observable</span>
    <span class="k">Determination source</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">customer-path synthetic check failures (impact provenance block)</span>
  </div>
