</section>


<div class="pmh">3 · What happened</div>

<section>
  <h2>Incident phases</h2>
  <table><thead><tr><th style="width:22%">Phase</th><th style="width:30%">When</th><th>What happened</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr>
    <td><b>Detection</b></td>
    <td>2026-07-12 18:12:00 UTC</td>
    <td>First anomalous evidence observed.</td>
  </tr><tr>
    <td><b>Degradation</b></td>
    <td>2026-07-12 18:12:00 UTC → 2026-07-12 18:16:00 UTC</td>
    <td>Anomalous evidence persisted across the participating evidence classes.</td>
  </tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note">Component recovery and service recovery are tracked separately; a component coming back never closes a service that is still failing.</div>
</section>


<section>
  <h2>How the failure propagated</h2>
  
  <div class="note">No causal sequence is proposed for this case — the engine has not matched a propagation pattern, and none is invented.</div>
  
  
  <div class="note">No alternative hypothesis carries evidence in this window.</div>
</section>


<div class="pmh">4 · Trigger</div>
<section>
  <p style="margin:4px 0 8px">Not determined. The engine does not distinguish the incident trigger (the event or change that set the failure off) from the earliest observed symptom, and no trigger has been causally established.</p>
  
  
</section>


<div class="pmh">5 · Root cause and contributing factors</div>
<section class="why">
  <h2>Analysis reasoning</h2>
  <p><b style="color:#b45309">Why suspected:</b> One active-check source reported degradation to the same target during an overlapping time window.</p>
  <p><b style="color:#475467">Why not confirmed:</b> Only active path measurement saw this — a second independent source is needed to confirm.</p>
  <p><b style="color:#1d4ed8">Required confirmation:</b> Identify whether the checks failed during DNS, TCP, TLS, or HTTP; validate vantage independence; and compare the incident window against real-user traffic, load-balancer health, application errors, and network telemetry.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Fault localization</h2>
  <p>The fault has not been localized to a specific domain or object.</p>
  
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Root cause</h2>
  <p>Root cause has not been identified.</p>
  
  <h2>Contributing factors</h2>
  <div class="note">Not determined. The engine does not yet separate contributing factors from alternative hypotheses; alternatives are listed under hypotheses and are never relabeled as contributing factors.</div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Current hypothesis</h2>
  
  <table><thead><tr><th style="width:4%">#</th><th style="width:32%">Hypothesis</th><th style="width:13%">Confidence</th><th style="width:27%">Supporting</th><th>Missing / to confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-weight:800">1</td>
    <td><b>Application / service experience change</b> <span class="pill gray" style="font-size:9px">symptom classification</span>
        
        <div class="note">condition: observed · causal role: symptom</div>
        <div class="note">candidate owner: Application team</div></td>
    <td>Suspected</td>
    <td>Synthetic http failure (2 observations); Packet loss (one observation)</td>
    <td>observe Traffic volume change</td>
  </tr>
  </tbody></table>
  
</section>


<div class="pmh">6 · Detection and response</div>
<section>
  <h2>Detection milestones</h2>
  
  <table><thead><tr><th style="width:28%">Milestone</th><th style="width:24%">When</th><th>Source of this timestamp</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr>
    <td><b>First credible failure</b></td>
    <td style="font-family:ui-monospace,monospace">2026-07-12 18:12:00 UTC</td>
    <td>earliest attached anomalous observation in the correlation window (observed)</td>
  </tr>
  </tbody></table>
  
  <div class="note">Not recorded: First service impact · First Correlix detection · First alert · First acknowledgement · First user/help-desk report · First mitigation · Service restoration · Recovery validation — a milestone without a sourced timestamp is stated as absent, never estimated.</div>
  
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Decision</h2>
  <div class="decision ">
    <b>Investigate</b> — Evidence is aligned but not independently confirmed. Validate the missing evidence before opening a customer incident.
  </div>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">Policy</span><span class="v">Default ServiceNow incident policy (platform default — no tenant policy configured)</span>
    <span class="k">Ticket-open threshold</span><span class="v">verdict ≥ suspected, customer-facing evidence required, suspected additionally requires critical severity</span>
    <span class="k">Monitoring window</span><span class="v">30m 00s after recovery</span>
    <span class="k">Auto-close</span><span class="v">no recurrence and no NEW customer-impact evidence arising within the monitoring window (impact already recorded for this incident stays recorded and does not block a clean close)</span>
    <span class="k">Reopen</span><span class="v">the same condition recurs within 30m 00s (flap suppression)</span>
    <span class="k">Escalation</span><span class="v">armed — triggers when customer impact is confirmed, or a second independent evidence class corroborates the fault</span>
    <span class="k">Ticket recommendation</span><span class="v">Hold — single active-probe plane — awaiting independent corroboration</span>
    
  
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">Triage owner</span><span class="v">NOC</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">Default triage owner until the failure stage and fault domain are identified.</span>
    <span class="k">Suspected fault domain</span><span class="v">Undetermined</span>
    
    
    <span class="k">Escalation owner</span><span class="v">Pending</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">Escalation owner is assigned when the analysis reaches probable/confirmed with a supported fault domain.</span>
  </div>
  
