  <tr><td>Application team</td><td>named by the &#34;Application / service experience change&#34; hypothesis (suspected)</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>


<div class="pmh">7 · Mitigation and service recovery</div>
<section>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">Recovery</span><span class="v">Not observed</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">No recovery evidence was captured.</span>
    <span class="k">Component recovery</span><span class="v">Not applicable</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">No component-scope evidence participated in this incident.</span>
    <span class="k">Service recovery</span><span class="v">Not observed</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">No service-level recovery evidence was captured.</span>
    <span class="k">Monitoring</span><span class="v">Not started</span>
  </div>
  <div class="note">Component recovery and service recovery are assessed separately. Mitigation steps appear in the detection milestones only when an operator or ITSM lifecycle stamp records them — they are never assumed.</div>
</section>


<div class="pmh">8 · Corrective actions</div>
<section>
  <h2>Immediate next actions</h2>
  <ol class="actions">
  <li><span class="pill red" style="font-size:9px">P1</span> <b>Inspect the most recent failed check transaction</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: DNS result, resolved IP, TCP status, TLS status, HTTP status, response time, and the failure stage</div></li>
  <li><span class="pill blue" style="font-size:9px">P2</span> <b>Compare real traffic, load-balancer target health and application errors during the incident window</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: request volume, completion rate, load-balancer target health, application error rate</div><div class="note">Escalate when: real-user impact, flow loss, or application errors corroborate the checks</div></li>
  <li><span class="pill blue" style="font-size:9px">P2</span> <b>Continue monitoring under the active policy</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: auto-close after the stability window, reopen on recurrence</div><div class="note">Escalate when: customer impact is confirmed, or a second independent evidence class corroborates the fault</div></li>
  <li><span class="pill blue" style="font-size:9px">P2</span> <b>Run the same check from an independent vantage (only prober-fra has reported this)</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: the same target&#39;s result from a second vantage — fails there too (target side) or only here (local side)</div></li>
  
  </ol>
  <div class="note">Durable corrective-action commitments (accountable owner, due date, success criteria, verification) are managed in the case's action register; a printed document is a status snapshot as of generation time.</div>
</section>


